  "extraction_notes": "[text-pass] The study focuses on AgSbTe2 thin films synthesized via melt-quenching and thermal evaporation, followed by post-deposition thermal annealing at various temperatures (50, 70, 90, 110 \u00b0C). No chemical dopants were added; the optimization approach was thermal annealing. [figure-pass p1-5] The provided pages do not contain any thermoelectric property-vs-temperature plots. Data was extracted from the abstract text. The samples are AgSbTe2 thin films subjected to different annealing temperatures (AST-AS is as-deposited, AST-90 is annealed at 90 C). [figure-pass p6-10] The provided pages contain structural, microstructural, Raman, and optical band gap characterization of AgSbTe2 thin films (samples AST-AS, AST-50, AST-70, AST-90, AST-110). However, there are no plots or tables reporting thermoelectric properties such as Seebeck coefficient, electrical conductivity, thermal conductivity, power factor, or ZT as a function of temperature. [figure-pass p11-14] The provided pages discuss AgSbTe2 thin films (labeled AST-AS, AST-50, AST-70, AST-90, AST-110) in the context of structural, morphological, and Hall effect characterization. While the text mentions that these samples exhibit p-type conduction consistent with a positive Seebeck coefficient, no plots or tables showing thermoelectric properties (Seebeck coefficient, electrical conductivity, thermal conductivity, power factor, or ZT) as a function of temperature are present in the provided images. ",
